//  (a) 21 of the ACTIVE registrations declare an HType format byte that does not
//      match the C++ type of the address they publish.  SecsSvEcRegistration
//      dereferences strictly by HType (`FT_8_TYPE` -> `*(double*)P`,
//      `INT_4_TYPE` -> `*(int*)P`, `BOOLEAN_TYPE` -> 1 byte; see
//      SecsSvEcRegistration.cpp:820-901), so each reads/writes the wrong width
//      at that address.  Measured against GOLDEN's own header declarations:
//        * 9 x INT_4_TYPE on a `bool` (1 byte) -- ECIDs 8538, 8564, 8571, 8578,
//          9558, 16000, 16002, 16110 (&tRotate.ActiveRotate), ...
//        * 8 x FT_8_TYPE on an `int` (4 bytes) -- ECIDs 16114-16117, 16122-16125
//          (&tRotate.RotateDutDate[...]): reads 8 bytes as a double out of a
